      "writtenOn": "2014-03-18T17:54:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "None does not equal False, but both are \"falsey\" if cast to a boolean first. for example, both of these are true:\n\n  None !\u003d False\n  bool(None) \u003d\u003d bool(False)\n\nand null is a reasonable default for any type of option, but users wouldn\u0027t be able to manually specify it in most cases",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAWH//UkE\u003d",
